As part of our team, you will be helping us create an entirely new network for the world's money.

For everyone, everywhere.

More about our mission and what we offer.

This is a senior, high-impact role in Wise's global Legal team, focused on corporate law, corporate governance and strategic transactions across a listed, multi-jurisdictional group. As a public company dual-listed on Nasdaq and the London Stock Exchange and operating across the UK, EMEA, the US and beyond, Wise's corporate agenda is broad and fast-moving. We cover a range of matters such as capital markets and disclosure, group M&A and corporate development, treasury and debt programmes, regulatory capital and licence applications, share plans and reward, and board and subsidiary governance. Your mission is to enable, protect and empower the business and people of Wise, helping the group achieve growth with minimal distraction.

You'll partner with senior stakeholders across the business and provide first-rate corporate legal advice as Wise continues to scale globally. To achieve this you'll be:

-
Providing strategic corporate law advice and practical, commercially-focused solutions to the group and its subsidiary entities across general corporate law and corporate governance, supporting both listed parent-company and regulated-subsidiary requirements;

-
Advising on capital markets and group disclosure matters, including periodic and ad hoc disclosure obligations, market abuse and inside information controls, and the corporate and securities-law aspects of operating a dual-listed structure;

-
Supporting capital raising and treasury activity, including equity matters and debt programmes, working closely with the Investor Relations, Treasury and group Finance functions;

-
Leading and supporting reorganisations and corporate development activity, working closely with the group strategy and corporate development teams, from structuring and drafting through to negotiation and completion;

-
Advising the group Finance function on the corporate and governance aspects of the group's consolidated annual report and accounts, and supporting board and committee reporting;

-
Advising Reward on the corporate and governance implications of share option and other equity incentive arrangements;

-
Supporting corporate governance across the group's entities, including board and subsidiary governance, intra-group arrangements, entity management and, where relevant, licence and regulatory-capital related corporate matters;

-
Preparing, reviewing and negotiating a broad range of corporate agreements and documents in connection with the group's corporate activities;

- Working as part of a team of generalist lawyers to support the wider commercial needs of the business, including advising on platform and partnership arrangements and drafting and negotiating a broad range of commercial agreements across Wise's products and business lines, from structuring and drafting through to negotiation;

-
Working proactively with the wider Legal team to build and scale a high-performing corporate legal advisory function, delivering a range of high-profile, enterprise-wide corporate transactions;

-
Leading and evolving corporate legal processes, procedures and governance-risk frameworks appropriate to a listed group, including through identifying technology solutions that streamline workflows and increase scalability;

-
Managing relationships with external counsel and suppliers to optimise cost, budget and value while securing top-quality legal support;

-
Understanding the real risks to the business and advising on the operational impact and practicalities of those risks; and

-
Mentoring and upskilling other members of the Legal team and the wider business, making life simple and easy.

